    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0431" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/12–1144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-11T21:00:00+01:00">December 11,
                            1944—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 11—6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10997. For attention of Mr. Dunn. Thank you for your 10249, December 7, in reply
                    to the last paragraph of my 10609, December 1.</p>
                <p>The directive on treatment of United Nations POW’s<anchor n="94" xml:id="d219-f1"
                    /> in Germany I am sure you realize involves political considerations as well as
                    military action. It therefore clearly falls within the category of directives
                    which we agreed in the conference with the War Department should be considered
                    by the EAC. Both you and McCloy were present at this meeting. My inability to
                    act is holding back the work of the committee authorized by the EAC to consider
                    this subject. The British, the Russians and the French are all ready to proceed.
                    I hope that the differences which you referred to in your message and which you
                    explained would be discussed at a higher level conference scheduled to meet on
                    December 9 have been resolved and that we may expect a reply the early part of
                    this week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d219-f1" n="94" xml:id="d219-f1-content">
                <p>Prisoners of War.</p>
            </note>
